.DS_Store
__pycache__/
**/test_package/build*/
**/test_package/CMakeUserPresets.json
.xmake/
build/

# Personal / device data — never tracked. Only the example is.
device.env*
device.*.env
!device.env.example

# Local screenshots may show device content
**/shots/
*-shots/
tests/backports/emulate/calls/xmake-addons.lock

# A hand-run Swift probe writes its compiled module next to the sources it was made from; a stale
# one there is what a later `-I` on that directory reads instead of the source. The recipes compile
# the module from the sources, so these are never needed (AGENTS.md, Conventions: build artifacts are
# never committed).
*.swiftmodule
*.swiftdoc
*.swiftsourceinfo
*.abi.json
tools/.media-player-include.m
tools/.media-player-include.m.ast

# The sibling of a file the generators' atomic writer (tools/atomic.lua) was writing when its process was killed.
*.charon-new.*

# The generated layer of the apple-backports package: written by tools/gen.lua from the committed spec/ snapshot at build time.
packages/a/apple-backports/.gen/
